post_install() {
    cat <<'EOF'
==> The Paseo desktop app already manages its own daemon (with your full
    shell env and DISPLAY), so most users do NOT need the systemd service.
    Only enable it if you want a persistent daemon for CLI/headless use:
        systemctl --user enable --now paseo.service
    Note: when started this way the daemon may lack DISPLAY/WAYLAND_DISPLAY,
    so agents launched through it cannot open GUI apps — use the desktop app
    for that. Do not enable-linger unless you really want it running while
    logged out.
EOF
}
